{"availability":"available","full":"NuoJohnChen/JudgeLRM","name":"JudgeLRM","description":"JudgeLRM: Large Reasoning Models as a Judge","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":43,"forks":3,"created":"2025-03-29T02:34:33Z","updated":"2026-05-06T08:08:22Z","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/nuojohnchen/JudgeLRMDemo","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.559Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.559Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.559Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.559Z","stars":43,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["📃 [Paper] • 💻 [Github] • 🤗 [Models] • [Playground]","JudgeLRM is a family of judgment-oriented Large Language Models (LLMs) designed to enhance evaluative reasoning through reinforcement learning (RL) with judge-wise, outcome-driven rewards. It demonstrates that judgment is inherently a reasoning-intensive task and addresses the limitations of supervised fine-tuning (SFT) in pair-wise evaluation. Notably, JudgeLRM-3B surpasses GPT-4, and JudgeLRM-7B outperforms DeepSeek-R1.","Explore JudgeLRM’s reasoning capabilities and detailed comparisons by testing it against other Hugging Face models with your own questions!"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuoJohnChen/JudgeLRM/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fde77bd8065b103dee8b0dee2cd2a17becc84aa6579dd7045d8d0264371ff1f6","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.667Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.667Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"📃 [Paper] • 💻 [Github] • 🤗 [Models] • [Playground]","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuoJohnChen/JudgeLRM/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"fde77bd8065b103dee8b0dee2cd2a17becc84aa6579dd7045d8d0264371ff1f6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuoJohnChen/JudgeLRM/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.667Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-05-